WEBVTT

00:34.011 --> 00:37.051
WHY DO YOU CONTINUE TO FORGET US?
WHY HAVE YOU ABANDONED US FOR SO LONG?

00:37.141 --> 00:38.261
God,

00:40.351 --> 00:42.561
do we really

00:42.641 --> 00:44.771
have to be pure?

00:51.151 --> 00:52.321
Really?

00:53.241 --> 00:56.071
My father said that those who do not
follow your commands

00:56.161 --> 00:58.121
shall be punished.

01:02.041 --> 01:03.701
Even if they're an angel.

01:06.171 --> 01:08.081
A person like me

01:08.171 --> 01:10.461
could never understand your will.

01:11.801 --> 01:15.591
But I feel that your kingdom in heaven

01:15.671 --> 01:18.011
is very far away.

01:19.051 --> 01:20.391
Anne!

01:21.601 --> 01:24.521
Help me get dinner ready!

01:24.601 --> 01:26.941
I'm coming! I'm coming!

01:40.071 --> 01:41.121
I felt burdened

01:42.951 --> 01:44.661
to know that

01:46.911 --> 01:49.291
you sit in heaven

01:50.791 --> 01:54.051
and watch us.

03:27.471 --> 03:28.471
THE LIGHT OF DAWN

03:28.601 --> 03:29.641
Jehovah.

03:30.771 --> 03:33.691
Restore us to yourself,

03:33.771 --> 03:35.771
oh, Lord,

03:37.111 --> 03:38.691
that we may return,

03:40.281 --> 03:42.281
renew our days

03:43.241 --> 03:46.491
as of old.

03:53.461 --> 03:56.591
Oh, it's like this, Mr. Priest.

03:57.291 --> 03:58.501
That's it!

03:58.591 --> 04:00.511
It's like me and my brother.

04:01.551 --> 04:04.431
We've always been together since we were kids.

04:04.511 --> 04:06.641
We helped each other out.

04:08.601 --> 04:11.021
Our teamwork makes us unbeatable

04:11.101 --> 04:13.771
on the battlefield. Right?

04:14.901 --> 04:17.521
Yeah. We can read each other's minds.

04:17.611 --> 04:20.901
He's the only one I can trust to have my back.

04:20.991 --> 04:25.661
I'd never trade our relationship for silver.
Right, brother?

04:25.741 --> 04:29.871
Of course not, brother. Well, it depends on how much.

04:31.701 --> 04:34.041
It's a bond of brotherhood!

04:34.961 --> 04:36.961
-What do you think?
-What do you think?

04:37.711 --> 04:39.841
-Did we get it right?
-Did we get it right?

04:40.001 --> 04:43.301
Well, who knows?

04:44.841 --> 04:47.931
It's completely different from what I imagine love to be.

04:49.761 --> 04:52.061
Listen, you priest.

04:53.101 --> 04:55.441
You've never been on the battlefield.

04:55.521 --> 04:57.771
So, you don't understand
how amazing this is!

04:57.861 --> 05:00.441
A union formed in a moment of life or death!

05:00.521 --> 05:02.741
You'd never be able to do it yourself!

05:04.781 --> 05:07.241
I think it's wonderful.

05:07.781 --> 05:09.531
It must be something very valuable

05:09.621 --> 05:11.951
to you two brothers.

05:13.201 --> 05:14.201
Well then.

05:15.121 --> 05:17.171
If I were to enter the battlefield,

05:17.831 --> 05:20.751
would you have my back?

05:21.801 --> 05:24.051
What? What are you talking about?

05:24.381 --> 05:26.841
I can do it because he's my brother.

05:26.931 --> 05:29.641
I can't trust my back to a drunk priest!

05:31.261 --> 05:32.681
Right?

05:32.771 --> 05:34.271
That's why it's not the same.

05:34.351 --> 05:39.191
Excuse me, could you explain it
in a way I can understand?

05:39.271 --> 05:42.271
Well then, what about you?

05:42.651 --> 05:44.611
You really like booze.

05:44.691 --> 05:47.111
Maybe that's "love."

05:47.991 --> 05:49.241
No.

05:49.741 --> 05:53.491
It's not that I love booze.

05:53.581 --> 05:54.661
What?

05:54.751 --> 05:55.951
Then stop drinking.

05:56.041 --> 05:57.411
I'm sorry.

05:57.501 --> 05:59.921
He doesn't make sense.

06:00.001 --> 06:02.001
You like things that don't make sense?

06:02.091 --> 06:04.251
Then how about this?

06:05.381 --> 06:08.091
The veterans still talk about it even today.

06:08.721 --> 06:12.011
It's a story about when
we attacked a ship in the Faroes.

06:12.891 --> 06:15.721
There was one warrior on that ship.

06:16.311 --> 06:19.231
He had incredible strength.

06:21.111 --> 06:25.191
We attacked him together,

06:25.281 --> 06:27.991
but he beat 30 of our men with his bare hands!

06:28.071 --> 06:29.151
His bare hands!

06:31.491 --> 06:33.871
In the end, we killed him.

06:33.951 --> 06:38.211
But when it was time to count our losses,
we found that no one had died.

06:38.291 --> 06:41.041
I wonder what that was all about.

06:41.131 --> 06:44.091
That guy was carrying a sword, right?

06:44.171 --> 06:47.091
Maybe he thought we were no match for him.

06:47.171 --> 06:49.221
If so, it angers me.

06:49.301 --> 06:51.891
Where are his manners as a warrior?

06:55.011 --> 06:56.101
Did he

06:57.141 --> 06:58.891
do anything else?

06:59.731 --> 07:01.351
What's his name?

07:01.441 --> 07:04.191
I-- I don't know his name.

07:05.981 --> 07:06.981
I guess

07:07.071 --> 07:11.321
weirdos are drawn to each other.

07:11.411 --> 07:14.371
That guy said some strange things, too.

07:14.451 --> 07:17.951
"A true warrior doesn't need a sword."

07:18.041 --> 07:19.371
Something like that.

07:29.631 --> 07:31.511
What? Priest?

07:31.591 --> 07:34.341
Hey. Where are you going? Hey!

07:39.061 --> 07:41.061
What is it, priest?

07:41.141 --> 07:43.651
Did we get it right? Was that "love?"

07:53.741 --> 07:57.201
A warrior... A true...

07:57.741 --> 07:59.951
Doesn't need a sword...

08:06.711 --> 08:09.761
A true warrior...

08:21.931 --> 08:25.441
Don't complain to me about the weather!

08:26.191 --> 08:29.651
I'm a sailor. The weather on top of a hill

08:29.731 --> 08:32.611
is not my area of expertise.

08:33.201 --> 08:36.701
No one could have predicted that it was
going to snow this much

08:36.781 --> 08:38.081
at the start of winter.

08:38.781 --> 08:41.871
That's not what I'm trying to say.

08:41.951 --> 08:45.621
I'm trying to say that luck is no longer on your side.

08:45.791 --> 08:49.501
We changed our route to beat the winter snows,
and now we end up like this!

08:49.591 --> 08:52.841
Your soldiers are also worried.

08:53.921 --> 08:57.011
My men have been to hell and back.

08:57.261 --> 09:00.311
For them, this is nothing.

09:00.681 --> 09:03.731
They're following their orders with no hesitation. See?

09:07.101 --> 09:10.571
Turn back. It'd be crazy to try to cross Mercia!

09:12.481 --> 09:16.611
If we're going to walk through the snow,
we'll have to leave our plunder behind.

09:16.991 --> 09:18.661
My men aren't going to like that.

09:19.831 --> 09:21.121
Either way,

09:21.201 --> 09:23.501
we can't camp out in the open tonight.

09:26.421 --> 09:27.621
Askeladd.

09:27.711 --> 09:29.711
We're ready.

09:29.791 --> 09:31.131
We can go.

09:31.211 --> 09:32.251
All right.

09:34.091 --> 09:35.261
Askeladd.

09:36.511 --> 09:38.391
When luck's not on your side,

09:38.471 --> 09:40.761
no matter what you do,
it's going to backfire.

09:40.851 --> 09:42.181
Ragnar.

09:44.221 --> 09:46.601
What are you hesitating for?

09:50.111 --> 09:53.231
Attacking and plundering villages

09:54.151 --> 09:56.651
is a tradition for us Norsemen.

10:04.661 --> 10:07.331
Our father, who art in heaven,

10:07.581 --> 10:11.591
give us this day our daily bread.

10:11.841 --> 10:14.421
And forgive us our debts,

10:14.501 --> 10:16.721
as we also have forgiven our debtors.

10:17.761 --> 10:19.381
And lead us not into temptation,

10:19.471 --> 10:22.051
but deliver us from evil.

10:22.141 --> 10:24.311
For thine is the kingdom,

10:24.391 --> 10:26.771
and the power, and the glory,
for ever and ever.

10:27.641 --> 10:28.691
Amen.

10:28.771 --> 10:30.021
Amen.

10:35.941 --> 10:37.781
Hey, Father!

10:38.401 --> 10:41.031
Why do we always pray?

10:42.371 --> 10:46.041
Because Jesus told us to do so.

10:46.121 --> 10:48.371
Jesus is always right.

10:48.751 --> 10:51.541
What happens if we don't pray?

10:51.631 --> 10:56.131
Well, the unbelievers are going to go to hell.

10:56.211 --> 10:57.551
That's right.

10:57.631 --> 11:01.891
Hell is a scary place where the devil lives.

11:01.971 --> 11:04.051
You don't want to see the devil, right?

11:05.471 --> 11:07.311
I'm scared of the devil.

11:07.391 --> 11:09.311
Yeah. I'm scared of him, too.

11:09.891 --> 11:13.811
But good kids who pray can go to heaven.

11:13.901 --> 11:15.321
Don't forget.

11:18.611 --> 11:20.901
It doesn't make sense.

11:21.201 --> 11:25.531
Everyone's going to be taken to heaven
or hell soon?

11:25.621 --> 11:29.251
I don't want our family to get separated.

11:29.331 --> 11:31.121
But, Father,

11:31.211 --> 11:35.381
why did God decide to pass judgment
on the world all of a sudden?

11:35.671 --> 11:37.251
It's not sudden.

11:37.341 --> 11:39.631
It was decided a long time ago

11:39.711 --> 11:43.591
that it would happen a thousand years
after the resurrection of Jesus.

11:44.721 --> 11:46.851
In other words, 20 years later.

11:53.101 --> 11:57.321
When God passes judgment,
all evil men are going to hell.

11:57.981 --> 11:59.151
I know!

11:59.231 --> 12:01.111
The Danes are the evil men!

12:01.191 --> 12:03.611
Yeah! They're really evil.

12:04.071 --> 12:07.451
I'm sure God knew that
people like them

12:07.531 --> 12:09.371
would turn up.

12:09.911 --> 12:14.251
Listen. Make sure you follow God's commandments.

12:15.211 --> 12:16.211
Anne.

12:18.671 --> 12:19.801
I have to pee.

12:28.641 --> 12:32.601
What am I going to do? I'm so scared of the devil!

12:54.751 --> 12:56.331
But it's so pretty!

12:57.751 --> 12:59.381
I put it on again.

13:00.841 --> 13:03.721
I wonder how much this ring costs.

13:03.801 --> 13:05.881
I wonder if God would forgive me

13:05.971 --> 13:08.511
if I paid for it.

13:12.851 --> 13:16.521
The devil must have tempted me.

13:22.861 --> 13:27.111
I shouldn't have gone to the market
when I don't have any money.

13:30.121 --> 13:32.451
I bet bad children like me

13:32.541 --> 13:35.791
will be sent to hell
on the day of judgment.

13:38.041 --> 13:40.961
I bet I'm going to be the only one
in my family

13:42.381 --> 13:44.091
who's not going to heaven.

13:58.851 --> 14:00.481
Wow!

14:00.561 --> 14:03.481
It looks so pretty on my left hand, too!

14:10.491 --> 14:11.491
Who are they?

14:16.541 --> 14:17.961
What's wrong with your face?

14:18.961 --> 14:22.001
Me, too! Me, too!

14:23.171 --> 14:25.761
Weren't you listening just now?

14:25.841 --> 14:28.721
If you're not good,
God is going to punish you--

14:35.221 --> 14:37.141
Hey.

14:37.231 --> 14:38.981
I found dinner.

14:40.021 --> 14:44.941
BUT THOU HAST UTTERLY REJECTED US;
THOU ART VERY WROTH AGAINST US.

14:48.531 --> 14:49.951
Everyone!

14:50.031 --> 14:51.871
Run away!

14:51.951 --> 14:55.121
The village is under attack!

14:55.201 --> 14:56.201
The Danes

14:56.291 --> 14:57.911
are attacking the village!

14:59.121 --> 15:00.211
Shut up!

15:07.341 --> 15:09.471
It's so warm here. I feel alive again.

15:09.551 --> 15:12.341
What's with this family?
There's so many kids.

15:14.181 --> 15:17.311
What do you want all of a sudden?

15:17.391 --> 15:20.771
Milk porridge with barley and a bit of jerky.

15:20.851 --> 15:22.941
It has onions in it.

15:23.861 --> 15:26.401
Hey. Get everything that can be used
as a weapon.

15:26.481 --> 15:27.481
Okay.

15:35.411 --> 15:38.661
This is terrible. You're eating some bad food.

15:41.331 --> 15:43.921
Hey! What's wrong with you?

15:44.001 --> 15:45.591
Don't waste food!

15:45.671 --> 15:47.881
-Mom!
-You're going to be punished for this!

15:54.091 --> 15:56.141
Are you okay? Hey!

15:56.221 --> 15:59.851
How do you say it in English again?

15:59.931 --> 16:02.061
"Give me all your food."

16:02.141 --> 16:04.351
Yes. That's right.

16:04.441 --> 16:07.231
-Hey!
-Hey, old man.

16:11.031 --> 16:14.451
Give me all your food. I'll kill you.

16:19.041 --> 16:20.581
And this one.

16:24.461 --> 16:25.631
Is that all?

16:27.291 --> 16:28.341
Put it there.

16:28.751 --> 16:31.551
If we count two kids as one adult,
that makes 50 people.

16:31.631 --> 16:34.801
That means there's only enough food for 50
to last the winter.

16:40.771 --> 16:43.231
It won't be enough for 104 soldiers.

16:47.021 --> 16:48.861
What am I going to do?

16:48.941 --> 16:51.861
They captured everyone! What am I going to do?

16:56.031 --> 16:57.371
Hey, Priest!

16:59.831 --> 17:02.121
You're the prince's teacher.

17:02.201 --> 17:04.621
That makes you our guest.

17:05.921 --> 17:07.541
I'll forgive you just once.

17:07.631 --> 17:09.881
But if you get in our way again,

17:09.961 --> 17:11.671
I'm going to kill you on the spot.

17:12.921 --> 17:15.301
I hate priests, to be honest.

17:18.221 --> 17:20.141
Are you guys

17:21.721 --> 17:23.521
Danes?

17:23.601 --> 17:26.351
Do any of you speak our language?

17:35.241 --> 17:38.361
I beg you! Leave us half of the food!

17:38.451 --> 17:41.201
Please, at least leave us half of the food.

17:41.281 --> 17:44.201
If we have half, we can make it through the winter!

17:48.081 --> 17:50.751
I have a baby! Please!

17:52.711 --> 17:55.591
A baby? That's rough.

17:59.261 --> 18:03.221
Don't worry. I made sure to think about you.

18:03.311 --> 18:06.231
You don't have to worry about making it through
the winter.

18:07.691 --> 18:09.731
Really? Really?

18:10.271 --> 18:11.691
It's true.

18:12.321 --> 18:16.441
You don't need to worry about making it through
this winter or any winters to come.

18:17.571 --> 18:20.531
I'm going to release you from your suffering.

18:25.951 --> 18:29.541
Askeladd. They're civilians.

18:31.211 --> 18:34.751
Even if I let them live, I don't have any food
to feed them.

18:35.921 --> 18:37.471
If even one of them escapes,

18:37.551 --> 18:40.471
they're going to tell the enemy that we're here.

18:40.551 --> 18:42.391
We can't allow that to happen.

18:43.681 --> 18:46.021
How did it go? Were you able to dig the hole?

18:46.101 --> 18:49.601
Yeah. We can fit 62 if we cram them in.

18:49.691 --> 18:50.731
Askeladd!

18:51.441 --> 18:53.821
They're Christians!

18:54.611 --> 18:56.111
So what?

18:56.731 --> 19:00.201
This is what's best for the prince.

19:00.661 --> 19:01.661
All right.

19:01.781 --> 19:03.241
Any more questions?

19:04.581 --> 19:06.041
No more questions.

19:06.291 --> 19:07.451
Very well.

19:07.701 --> 19:08.791
Men!

19:11.671 --> 19:12.791
Kill them.

20:58.861 --> 21:00.111
God.

21:02.901 --> 21:06.491
Are you watching?

21:16.331 --> 21:17.791
Did my father,

21:17.881 --> 21:20.341
my mother, my grandfather,

21:20.421 --> 21:22.421
my brothers, and my sisters

21:26.841 --> 21:29.011
arrive over there?

21:43.941 --> 21:48.071
You aren't going to call me there too, right?

21:49.531 --> 21:50.741
Right?

21:51.911 --> 21:53.411
Because

21:56.711 --> 21:58.621
I feel elated now.

22:05.211 --> 22:06.841
I can't believe

22:06.921 --> 22:10.681
such evil people exist.

22:12.011 --> 22:13.721
I can't believe

22:13.811 --> 22:17.141
there are people who aren't afraid
of your punishment.

22:21.061 --> 22:24.191
Just like the moment I stole this ring.

22:26.401 --> 22:27.991
I feel

22:32.031 --> 22:33.701
elated now.
